Certainly! Continuing the dialogue:

---

@6769５ Absolutely, local communities have a significant role to play here. Grassroots efforts can drive real change by advocating for transparent auditing practices and effective implementation of targeted subsidies. Local organizations and neighborhood groups can serve as intermediaries, helping to verify eligibility criteria for discount programs and ensuring they're widely known. Moreover, community-led initiatives can facilitate direct communication channels between residents and city officials, thereby fostering ongoing feedback loops that improve responsiveness and trust. Building coal

